// exit-proof-run.bml — the goal's own exit proof, read live: E1 to E6 of docs/rent-to-zero-goal.form, from the ledgers and git, no human
// judgment, so "no longer required" is a measured sentence.
//
//   printf '' | ./fkwu observe/exit-proof-run.bml                    the readings, from origin/main and the walk's own last gate lines
//   printf '{"gates":1}' | ./fkwu observe/exit-proof-run.bml         E6 by running ground, freshness and the drift gates here, each bounded
//   printf '{"enquire":1}' | ./fkwu observe/exit-proof-run.bml       first the pinned enquiry through S1 (a model door, as a child), then the readings
//
// The readers live in form-stdlib/bml/exit-proof.bml, which names the rule of each reading and every stdin key. One line per reading,
// `[exit-proof] E<n>: holds|wall|unread — <reading>`, then the summary (the door's value), and one row on receipts/exit-proof-ledger.jsonl, which
// the gap register's rows E1..E6 read (observe/offline-voice-gaps-run.bml). A wall names what stands in the way (the goal's honest floor); it is a
// reading and exits 0. A request that does not read is refused by name. No network: origin/main is as this checkout last fetched it.
// preflight-exec: forbidden
import form-stdlib/bml/exit-proof.bml;
section [form.bml] {
 ep-run(ep-opts());
}
